course: dictionary
lesson: 13463
title: Humorous, not humourous
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: This word catches many writers out. The correct spelling is «humorous», with no «u» after the «o». The noun «humour» has a «u» in British English, so it is easy to add the «u» to the adjective by mistake.
explain: «Humorous» means funny, or meant to make people laugh. «The clown told a humorous story, and the whole class giggled.» A humorous story is a story that makes you laugh. If you see «humourous» in your writing, it is a misspelling, so take the «u» out.
explain: A quick check: the noun is «humour», so the feeling of funny is humour. The adjective that describes something funny is «humorous». Writers in every country spell the adjective the same way, even in the USA, where the noun is spelled «humor».
fact: «Humorous» means funny, or meant to make people laugh.
fact: The correct spelling is «humorous», with no «u» after the «o».
fact: The adjective is spelled «humorous» everywhere, including the USA.
fact: The noun «humour» has a «u» in the UK, Canada, Australia, New Zealand and Ireland.
fact: Two phrases you will see are «a humorous story» and «a humorous poem».
exercise: Which spelling is correct for a funny story? | humourous | *humorous | humerous | humorus
exercise: «The clown told a humorous story, and the whole class laughed.» What does humorous mean? | *Funny, meant to make people laugh | Loud and angry | Sad and quiet | Very old
exercise: Which sentence is spelled correctly? | «The dog wore a humerous hat.» | *«The dog wore a humorous hat.» | «The dog wore a humourous hat.» | «The dog wore a humorus hat.»
test: Which word is the adjective meaning funny? | Humour | Humble | *Humorous | Humid
test: «Grandma loves a humorous film about a talking cat.» What does humorous mean in this sentence? | Scary | Very large | Sleepy | *Funny
exam: Mia wrote a ___ poem about her dog, and everyone giggled. Choose the correct word. | *humorous | humerous | humourous | humorus
